content.text:
I've updated the #2600 card on the [PR Desk](https://claude.ai/artifact/UohxsGPhGM6VveP4w7ayvo). It now moves from "Needs your call" to "Request changes", and the open question is gone because you've ruled.

- **Findings:** they now explain where CIS v7 disagrees with itself:
  - the UI audit and remediation say there should be no app exclusions;
  - the Graph audit for 5.2.2.1, 5.2.2.2 and 5.2.2.5 doesn't check exclusions;
  - 5.2.2.2 recommends excluding the Rights Management Services app.
- **Draft comment:** it acknowledges why the author read it that way, then asks for four things:
  - keep the `No excluded applications` condition;
  - allow the Rights Management Services app (`00000012-0000-0000-c000-000000000000`) in 5.2.2.2;
  - list the excluded apps in the result;
  - update the guides and unit tests to match.
- **Optional fix, unticked:** we make those changes on the branch ourselves instead of waiting for the author. If you tick it, edit the comment so it says what we did rather than asking him to do it.

Nothing is posted to GitHub until you queue the card and tell me to process the desk.

