{
  "headSha": "dbac39f78319",
  "verdict": "decision",
  "summary": "Out of draft. CIS.GH.1.2.3 and 1.2.4 (repository and issue deletion) always return Investigate on main. This PR gives them a real assessment against a new sensitive `GlobalSettings.GitHubDeletionPolicy` (approved owner IDs, a per-repository approved admin roster, at most 3 owners, exactly 2 admins per repository). It also fixes types in 1.2.2, 1.3.2 and 1.3.8, rewrites the shared GitHub transport (rate-limit circuit breaker, 30 s timeouts, GraphQL), and changes the redaction and export pipeline for every suite, including a new public `Add-MtTestResultDetail -RedactedResult`. Evidence handling is sound: partial data never passes.",
  "question": "Should 1.2.3 and 1.2.4 fail out of the box (any org with 3+ owners fails every repository, and without config the checks can never pass), or stay Investigate until GitHubDeletionPolicy is configured? Do you accept -RedactedResult as public API and the change to the all-suite redaction pipeline, or ask for a split?",
  "findings": [
    {
      "sev": "high",
      "text": "Out-of-the-box change. On main both checks always return Investigate. With no config: more than 3 owners fails the owner branch, and in the repository branch (member deletion is on by default) any repository with more than 2 effective admins fails. Org owners count, so an org with 3+ owners fails every repository. Without config the checks can never pass. Verified.",
      "where": "powershell/internal/checks/cis/github/Test-MtCisGitHubDeletion.ps1:54,109"
    },
    {
      "sev": "medium",
      "text": "The repository branch lists the collaborators of every repository even when no policy exists and a pass is impossible: thousands of REST calls on a large org, on every run.",
      "where": "Test-MtCisGitHubDeletion.ps1:97-117"
    },
    {
      "sev": "medium",
      "text": "Scope: the export and redaction pipeline for all suites (`Invoke-Maester.ps1:1031,1097`, `Get-MtHtmlReport.ps1:150-159`, new `ConvertTo-MtRedactedResult`), plus the GitHub transport and rate-limit rewrite. 52 files; each part deserves its own review."
    },
    {
      "sev": "medium",
      "text": "Public API: new `-RedactedResult` on `Add-MtTestResultDetail` and a `TestResultRedacted` result field. The field is still exported when redaction is off, and `ConvertTo-MtRedactedResult` throws on bad imported values instead of falling back.",
      "where": "powershell/public/run/Add-MtTestResultDetail.ps1:101-109,250; powershell/internal/report/ConvertTo-MtRedactedResult.ps1:35-41"
    },
    {
      "sev": "medium",
      "text": "Hard rules: exactly 2 admins per repository, and `ValidateRange(1,3)` on `MaximumOrganizationOwners`. Unclear whether \"exactly two\" is CIS audit wording; an org whose policy allows 4+ owners can't configure it.",
      "where": "Test-MtCisGitHubDeletion.ps1:10,109"
    },
    {
      "sev": "low",
      "text": "Fail-fast after any rate limit, plus a 30 s read timeout, now applies to every GitHub check; an unknown reset time needs a reconnect.",
      "where": "powershell/internal/services/github/Invoke-MtGitHubRateLimitGuard.ps1"
    },
    {
      "sev": "low",
      "text": "Commits generated docs: `website/docs/tests/cis/CIS.GH.1.2.{2,3,4}.md`, `CIS.GH.1.3.{2,8}.md` and `website/docs/commands/Add-MtTestResultDetail.mdx`."
    },
    {
      "sev": "nit",
      "text": "A BOM was added to `Clear-ModuleVariable.ps1` with no other change; the PR body still says CI isn't green.",
      "where": "powershell/internal/session/Clear-ModuleVariable.ps1:1"
    }
  ],
  "comment": "Thanks @thetechgy. The evidence handling here is careful: partial lists can only prove a failure, missing data ends up as Skipped or Investigate and never as a pass, and the deletion guide is thorough.\n\nBefore we can merge, a few things need a change or a decision.\n\n- **Blocking: out-of-the-box result for CIS.GH.1.2.3 and 1.2.4.** On main these always return Investigate. With this PR and no config, many orgs will fail:\n  - Org owners are effective admins on every repository. With member deletion enabled (GitHub's default), any org with three or more owners fails every repository.\n  - An org with more than three owners fails the owner check.\n\n  Without `GitHubDeletionPolicy` the checks can never pass. I'd like them to stay Investigate until approvals are configured, and fail only once the config exists.\n- **Blocking: API cost.** With member deletion enabled, the check lists collaborators for every repository even when no config exists and a pass is impossible. On a large org that's thousands of calls on every run. Please stop after the inventory read with Investigate when the policy, or its `Repositories` list, is missing.\n- **Blocking: please split the PR.** It changes much more than the GitHub CIS checks:\n  - the export and redaction pipeline every suite uses (`Invoke-Maester`, `Get-MtHtmlReport`, `ConvertTo-MtRedactedResult`);\n  - a new public parameter, `Add-MtTestResultDetail -RedactedResult`;\n  - the shared GitHub transport (rate-limit guard, timeouts, metadata and GraphQL helpers).\n\n  Each of these needs its own review. A suggested split:\n  1. the 1.2.2, 1.3.2 and 1.3.8 type fixes, which could merge quickly;\n  2. GitHub transport and rate limiting;\n  3. redacted results;\n  4. the deletion checks and `GitHubDeletionPolicy`.\n- **Question: \"exactly two administrators\" and the 1-3 owner cap.** Is \"exactly two\" the benchmark's audit wording? If not, please make it configurable or soften it. Capping `MaximumOrganizationOwners` at 3 also means an org whose policy allows more owners can't configure that.\n- **For the redacted-results PR:**\n  - `TestResultRedacted` is still written to JSON and HTML when redaction is off. Please leave it out of those.\n  - For imported results, please fall back to the generic redaction rather than throwing on an invalid value.\n- **Optional:**\n  - Please drop the changes to generated files (`website/docs/tests/cis/*.md`, `website/docs/commands/Add-MtTestResultDetail.mdx`); automation regenerates them.\n  - Please remove the BOM added to `Clear-ModuleVariable.ps1`.\n  - Please update the PR description now that CI is green.",
  "ci": "passing"
}
