That confirms the cause: throttling, not #2625. Run on its own, ASD.ISM-1648 on #2625 lists all 9 users, the same 9 that main listed, including AdeleV, annaj and MeganB. So the #2625 changes match main on every check in the elapora tenant.

The earlier gap is still a real bug, already on main. When Graph throttles part of a batched call, the users in the throttled part are dropped without any warning. A check can then report fewer problems than the tenant really has, as ASD.ISM-1648 just did. The fix would be in `Invoke-MtGraphRequest`:
- retry a throttled item after the wait Graph asks for;
- keep skipping objects that return 404, as it does today;
- raise an error for anything else.

